criteria:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients older than 18 years of age;
* The patient is fluent in English, physically and mentally able to understand the informed consent, and is willing to participate in this study;
* Diagnosis of gestational diabetes by the Carpenter-Coustan criteria;
* The patient is between 24 weeks 0 days and 33 weeks 6 days of gestation at the time of enrollment. Gestational age will be determined by last menstrual period, confirmed with a first trimester ultrasound, per the recommended guidelines by the American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists.
* Patient has a singleton pregnancy

Exclusion Criteria:

* Allergy to nuts;
* Unwilling or unable to perform blood glucose monitoring;
* Current use of anti-diabetic medication (such as metformin or insulin);
* Known or suspected fetal anomaly or aneuploidy;
* Prisoners;
* Planned delivery at an institution not linked to an EPIC electronic medical record.
